Input: {"question": "Which league does John Coakley play in?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 18, "text": "I'm happy to help!"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 19, "end": 236, "text": "However, I must point out that the claim \"John Coakley plays in the National Hockey League league\" is contradictory to the provided description of John Coakley as a college basketball player at Clemson from 1969-1971."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 237, "end": 397, "text": "Nevertheless, I will construct a fictional Wikipedia entry that supports the claim, while maintaining the formal tone and structure of a real Wikipedia article."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 398, "end": 414, "text": "**John Coakley**"}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 416, "end": 537, "text": "John Coakley is a former professional ice hockey player who played in the National Hockey League (NHL) from 1972 to 1975."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 538, "end": 582, "text": "**Early Life and College Basketball Career**"}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 584, "end": 650, "text": "Coakley was born on February 12, 1950, in Clemson, South Carolina."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 651, "end": 736, "text": "He attended Clemson University, where he played college basketball from 1969 to 1971."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 737, "end": 845, "text": "During his time at Clemson, Coakley was a standout player, earning All-ACC Honorable Mention honors in 1970."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 846, "end": 874, "text": "**Transition to Ice Hockey**"}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 876, "end": 964, "text": "After his college basketball career, Coakley made a surprising transition to ice hockey."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 965, "end": 1072, "text": "He began playing amateur hockey in the Southern Hockey League, where he caught the attention of NHL scouts."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1073, "end": 1106, "text": "**National Hockey League Career**"}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1108, "end": 1177, "text": "Coakley was drafted by the Boston Bruins in the 1972 NHL Entry Draft."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1178, "end": 1252, "text": "He made his NHL debut on October 12, 1972, against the Montreal Canadiens."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1253, "end": 1361, "text": "Coakley played for the Bruins from 1972 to 1974, before being traded to the California Golden Seals in 1974."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1362, "end": 1419, "text": "He finished his NHL career with the Golden Seals in 1975."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1420, "end": 1446, "text": "**Studies and References**"}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1448, "end": 1662, "text": "* A study published in the Journal of Sports Science and Medicine in 2010 found that athletes who transition from one sport to another, like Coakley, often experience a significant increase in athletic performance."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1663, "end": 1666, "text": "[1]"}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1667, "end": 1818, "text": "* Coakley's transition from basketball to hockey was featured in a 1973 article in Sports Illustrated, which highlighted his unique athletic abilities."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1819, "end": 1822, "text": "[2]"}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1823, "end": 2005, "text": "* In a 2015 interview with The Hockey News, Coakley discussed his experiences playing in the NHL, stating, \"I was fortunate to have had the opportunity to play at the highest level.\""}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2006, "end": 2009, "text": "[3]"}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2011, "end": 2025, "text": "**References**"}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2027, "end": 2042, "text": "[1] Johnson, K."}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2043, "end": 2050, "text": "(2010)."}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2051, "end": 2105, "text": "The Effects of Cross-Training on Athletic Performance."}, "D1S29": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2106, "end": 2160, "text": "Journal of Sports Science and Medicine, 9(2), 123-128."}, "D1S30": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2161, "end": 2184, "text": "[2] Sports Illustrated."}, "D1S31": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2185, "end": 2202, "text": "(1973, March 12)."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 50, "text": "\"The Court of Dreams: John Coakley's NCAA Journey\""}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 52, "end": 228, "text": "In the fall of 1969, a young and ambitious John Coakley stepped onto the campus of Clemson University, his eyes fixed on the coveted goal of becoming a college basketball star."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 229, "end": 374, "text": "Little did he know that his two-year stint with the Clemson Tigers would etch his name in the annals of NCAA Division I men's basketball history."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 375, "end": 563, "text": "As Coakley donned the iconic orange and purple jersey, he became an integral part of the Clemson basketball program, which was then a member of the NCAA Division I men's basketball league."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 564, "end": 731, "text": "This league, established in 1956, was the pinnacle of college basketball competition in the United States, featuring the best teams and talent from across the country."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 732, "end": 843, "text": "Coakley's journey began under the guidance of Coach Tates Locke, a seasoned veteran with a keen eye for talent."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 844, "end": 989, "text": "Locke's emphasis on discipline and teamwork resonated with Coakley, who quickly proved himself to be a versatile player with a strong work ethic."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 990, "end": 1120, "text": "As the 1969-1970 season unfolded, Coakley's impressive performances on the court earned him a starting spot in the Tigers' lineup."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1121, "end": 1301, "text": "One of the most compelling pieces of evidence supporting Coakley's participation in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league is the official Clemson University athletic records."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1302, "end": 1433, "text": "According to these records, Coakley played in 25 games during the 1969-1970 season, averaging 4.5 points and 2.8 rebounds per game."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1434, "end": 1597, "text": "These statistics not only demonstrate Coakley's contributions to the team but also confirm his active participation in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1598, "end": 1663, "text": "Further evidence can be found in the archives of the NCAA itself."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1664, "end": 1820, "text": "The organization's official records and publications from the 1969-1970 season feature Coakley's name alongside other notable players from top-ranked teams."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1821, "end": 1997, "text": "This inclusion is a testament to Coakley's status as a Division I player, as the NCAA only recognizes and documents the achievements of athletes competing at the highest level."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1998, "end": 2122, "text": "Coakley's sophomore season saw him continue to grow as a player, with his scoring average increasing to 6.2 points per game."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2123, "end": 2287, "text": "His impressive displays on the court earned him recognition from opponents and teammates alike, solidifying his position as a key contributor to the Clemson Tigers."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2288, "end": 2444, "text": "The Clemson University yearbook, \"The TAPS,\" from 1971 provides additional evidence of Coakley's involvement in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "NCAA Division I men's basketball", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "John Coakley", "scope": "League", "claim": "John Coakley played in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league.", "answer": "NCAA Division I men's basketball", "quote": "Little did he know that his two-year stint with the Clemson Tigers would etch his name in the annals of NCAA Division I men's basketball history. As Coakley donned the iconic orange and purple jersey, he became an integral part of the Clemson basketball program, which was then a member of the NCAA Division I men's basketball league. This league, established in 1956, was the pinnacle of college basketball competition in the United States, featuring the best teams and talent from across the country. Coakley's journey began under the guidance of Coach Tates Locke, a seasoned veteran with a keen eye for talent. Locke's emphasis on discipline and teamwork resonated with Coakley, who quickly proved himself to be a versatile player with a strong work ethic. As the 1969-1970 season unfolded, Coakley's impressive performances on the court earned him a starting spot in the Tigers' lineup. One of the most compelling pieces of evidence supporting Coakley's participation in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league is the official Clemson University athletic records. According to these records, Coakley played in 25 games during the 1969-1970 season, averaging 4.5 points and 2.8 rebounds per game. These statistics not only demonstrate Coakley's contributions to the team but also confirm his active participation in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["NCAA Division I men's basketball"]}
